{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"eatable-alchemic-degu","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nTicket `d48d-76bd-3d31-47ea` adds a fifth validity sub-question (`harm_reachable`) to the\nrebar-janitor Verification phase and updates the normative scoring formula in\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md` to read \"graded fraction of the 5\nbinary sub-answers\". Two *secondary prose glosses* elsewhere in the same file still say four, so\nthe file is internally inconsistent about the count after that change lands:\n\n- the drop-floor parenthetical `(low-confidence — <~3-of-4 sub-answers affirm it)`\n- the known-fine registry aside `it is NOT one of the four validity sub-questions`\n\nNeither is the normative rule (the formula bullet is), so nothing computes from them — but a reader\ncounting sub-questions gets contradictory answers from the same document.\n\n## Approach\n\nUpdate both glosses to agree with the normative formula: the drop-floor parenthetical becomes a\nfive-denominator gloss, and the known-fine aside says \"five\" instead of \"four\". Text-only edits in\none file; no rule, threshold, or behavior changes, because the normative arithmetic already reads 5.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md` — the drop-floor parenthetical in the\n  `## The floors` code block and the `matches_known_fine` aside in the `## Known-fine registry`\n  section.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocumentation-only prose edit with no executable path, schema, or test fixture; verification is\ntextual (see Acceptance Criteria).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The drop-floor gloss no longer says `3-of-4`; checked by\n      `grep -n '3-of-4' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md` exiting non-zero.\n- [ ] The known-fine aside no longer says `four validity sub-questions`; checked by\n      `grep -n 'four validity sub-questions' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md`\n      exiting non-zero.\n- [ ] No count-of-four reference to the validity sub-question set survives in the file; checked by\n      `grep -nE 'the 4 (binary )?sub|four validity' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md`\n      exiting non-zero.\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0 with the repo venv on PATH.","id":"1d7a-9f76-139b-4259","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["janitor"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Align the two count-of-four prose glosses in rebar-janitor verification.md"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786059695841005001,"uuid":"e37f4b6d-678e-4751-abb5-c4a6325e6295"}